    "content": "James Ewen | About | Imperial College London\n\n[![Imperial College London homepage](data:image/svg+xml;base64,)](/)\n\n[Skip to main content](#profile-tab-menu)[All experts](/search?type=user)\n\n![](/j.ewen/thumbnail)\n\n# DrJames Ewen\n\nHonorary Research Fellow\n\nDepartment of Mechanical Engineering - Faculty of Engineering\n\n-   Contact\n-   External links\n-   View collaborators\n\nOrcid identifier[0000-0001-5110-6970 (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5110-6970)\n\n-   Honorary Research Fellow\n    \n    Department of Mechanical Engineering - Faculty of Engineering\n    \n\n-   [j.ewen@imperial.ac.uk (opens in a new tab)](mailto:j.ewen@imperial.ac.uk)\n    \n-   [j.ewen14@imperial.ac.uk (Work) (opens in a new tab)](mailto:j.ewen14@imperial.ac.uk)\n    \n\n-   462, City and Guilds Building, South Kensington Campus, United Kingdom\n\n-   Collaboration Network\n\n-   [Affiliations – Applied Mechanics (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/mechanical-engineering/research/applied-mechanics)\n    \n-   [Affiliations – CDT in Chemical Biology: Innovation in Life Sciences (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/chemical-biology/cdt)\n    \n-   [Affiliations – CDT in Chemical Biology: Innovation in Life Sciences - supervisor (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/chemical-biology/cdt/about-us/supervisors)\n    \n-   [Affiliations – Energy Futures Lab Affiliate (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/energy-futures-lab)\n    \n-   [Affiliations – Institute for Molecular Science and Engineering (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/molecular-science-engineering)\n    \n-   [Affiliations – Institute of Chemical Biology (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/chemical-biology)\n    \n-   [Affiliations – Tribology (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.imperial.ac.uk/tribology)\n    \n-   [Energy Futures Lab (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/energy-futures-lab/)\n    \n-   [Google Scholar (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://scholar.google.co.uk/citations?user=hW5_woUAAAAJ&amp;hl=en)\n    \n-   [Linkedin (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.linkedin.com/in/james-ewen/)\n    \n-   [ORCID (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5110-6970)\n    \n-   [Publons (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://publons.com/author/1168866/james-p-ewen#profile)\n    \n-   [RAEng Research Fellowship (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.raeng.org.uk/grants-prizes/grants/support-for-research/raeng-research-fellowship/current-and-recent-awards)\n    \n-   [ResearcherID (opens in a new tab)⁠](http://www.researcherid.com/rid/O-9499-2017)\n    \n-   [Researchgate (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/James_Ewen2)\n    \n\n[\n\nAre you James Ewen?\n\nEdit your profile\n\n\n\n](https://symplectic.imperial.ac.uk/userprofile.html?uid=86996)\n\n-   ABOUT\n    \n-   [PUBLICATIONS](/j.ewen/publications)\n    \n-   [PROFESSIONAL ACTIVITIES](/j.ewen/professional)\n    \n-   MORE\n    \n\n## BIO\n\nDr. James P. Ewen is a Lecturer in Mechanical Engineering at the University of Bath. He is also an Honorary Research Fellow in the Department of Mechanical Engineering, Imperial College London. He was formerly an Royal Academy of Engineering (RAEng) Research Fellow in the same department. He is a Chartered Engineer (CEng) and a Member of the Institution of Mechanical Engineers (IMechE). He is also a Fellow of the Higher Education Academy (FHEA).  \n  \nJames uses supercomputers to study solid-liquid interfaces with molecular simulations. He studies complex formulations to identify links between their nanoscale behaviour and macroscale performance. His research is highly interdisciplinary in nature and is of direct relevance to industry. James has worked with many large multinational companies (Shell, SKF, Afton Chemical, Baker Hughes, Repsol, and Procter & Gamble), scientific software specialists (Scienomics, NextMol, and SCM), and other institutions (Natural History Museum, Diamond Light Source, and DSTL) to help to solve engineering grand challenges. He has also collaborated with researchers from academic institutions all over the world, including ETH Zürich, University of Bologna, University of Saarland, TU Delft, Politecnico di Milano, RMIT University, King's College London, Brunel University London, University of California Merced, University of Alabama, California Institute of Technology, Pennsylvania State University, and the University of Pennsylvania. He is also a Visiting Research Fellow at Swinburne University of Technology, Australia. He is an Affiliate of the Institute of Molecular Science and Engineering (IMSE) and the Energy Futures Lab at Imperial College London as well as the Thomas Young Centre: The London Centre for Theory and Simulation of Materials. He is currently an Assistant Supervisor to six PhD students. He is a co-organiser of the Web Seminar Series on Tribology (WeSST) and the UK Fluids Network Special Interest Group in Non-Equilibrium Molecular Dynamics (NEMD-SIG).\n\n  \nIn 2022, he received the inaugural Wen Shizhu Maple Leaf Award - International Young Scholar Award from the State Key Laboratory of Tribology at Tsinghua University. In 2020, he was awarded a RAEng Research Fellowship for the project 'Controlling Friction through Molecular Engineering'. He was awarded the Innovation in Tribology Award by the Institute of Physics (IOP) in 2019 and the Tribology Bronze Medal in 2018 by the IMechE. In 2017, he received a Doctoral Prize Fellowship from the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council (EPSRC). In the same year, he was awarded the Margaret Fishenden Centenary Memorial Prize for the best PhD Thesis in the Department of Mechanical Engineering over the previous five-year period.  \n  \nHe completed his PhD in the Tribology Group at Imperial College London, under the supervision of Prof. Daniele Dini and Prof. Hugh Spikes in 2017. His iCASE PhD studentship was co-funded by Shell and the EPSRC and he spent 15-months placed in Shell technology centres around the world during his undergraduate and post-graduate studies. He graduated from the University of Bath with a Masters in Chemistry degree (First Class Hons.) in 2014.\n\n## ACADEMIC POSITIONS\n\n-   Lecturer\n    \n    University of Bath, Mechanical Engineering, United Kingdom1 Oct 2025 - present\n    \n-   Honorary Research Fellow\n    \n    Imperial College London, Mechanical Engineering, United Kingdom1 Oct 2025 - present\n    \n-   RAEng Research Fellow\n    \n    Imperial College London, Mechanical Engineering, United Kingdom1 Oct 2020 - 30 Sep 2025\n    \n-   Research Associate\n    \n    Imperial College London, Mechanical Enginnering, London, United Kingdom1 Oct 2017 - 1 Oct 2020\n    \n\n## DEGREES\n\n-   PhD\n    \n    Imperial College London, UK1 Oct 2014 - 1 Oct 2017\n    \n-   MChem\n    \n    University of Bath, Bath, Bath, United Kingdom1 Oct 2010 - 1 Aug 2014\n    \n\n## FACULTY\n\n-   Faculty of Engineering\n    \n\n## POSITION NAME\n\n-   Honorary Research Fellow\n    \n\n## FIELDS OF RESEARCH\n\n-   Mechanical engineering\n-   Materials engineering\n-   Condensed matter physics\n-   Physical chemistry\n-   Nanotechnology\n-   Atomic and molecular physics\n-   Theoretical and computational chemistry\n-   Tribology\n-   Physical properties of materials\n-   Theory and design of materials\n-   Functional materials\n-   Macromolecular and materials chemistry\n\n![Imperial College London logo](data:image/svg+xml;base64,)\n\nImperial College London South Kensington Campus London SW7 2AZ\n\n+44 (0)20 7589 5111\n\n[»Report an issue via the service desk (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://servicemgt.imperial.ac.uk/ask)\n\n-   [»Visit Imperial (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/visit/)\n-   [»Study at Imperial (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/study/)\n-   [»Faculties and departments (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/faculties-and-departments/)\n-   [»What's on (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/whats-on/)\n-   [»News (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/news)\n-   [»Jobs (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/jobs/)\n\n-   [»About Imperial (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/about/)\n-   [»Research and innovation (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/research-and-innovation/)\n-   [»Leadership and strategy (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/about/leadership-and-strategy/)\n-   [»Support for partners and business (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/research-and-innovation/support-for-partners/)\n-   [»Accessibility (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/about-the-site/accessibility/imperial-profiles/)\n-   [»Cookie policy (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/about-the-site/use-of-cookies/)\n-   [»Media Team (opens in a new tab)⁠](https://www.imperial.ac.uk/media/contacts/)\n\n[Powered bySymplectic, part of Digital Science (opens in a new tab)](https://symplectic.co.uk)"
